  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 18,
  "sortOrder": 20018,
  "verseCount": 24,
  "aliases": [
    "Prov",
    "Pr",
    "Prv"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Through desire a man, having separated himself, seeketh and intermeddleth with all wisdom.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "A fool hath no delight in understanding, but that his heart may discover itself.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "When the wicked cometh, then cometh also contempt, and with ignominy reproach.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "The words of a man’s mouth are as deep waters, and the wellspring of wisdom as a flowing brook.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "It is not good to accept the person of the wicked, to overthrow the righteous in judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "A fool’s lips enter into contention, and his mouth calleth for strokes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "A fool’s mouth is his destruction, and his lips are the snare of his soul.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "The words of a talebearer are as wounds, and they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "He also that is slothful in his work is brother to him that is a great waster.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "The name of the LORD is a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "The rich man’s wealth is his strong city, and as an high wall in his own conceit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Before destruction the heart of man is haughty, and before honour is humility.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "He that answereth a matter before he heareth it, it is folly and shame unto him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "The spirit of a man will sustain his infirmity; but a wounded spirit who can bear?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "The heart of the prudent getteth knowledge; and the ear of the wise seeketh knowledge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "A man’s gift maketh room for him, and bringeth him before great men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "He that is first in his own cause seemeth just; but his neighbour cometh and searcheth him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "The lot causeth contentions to cease, and parteth between the mighty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "A brother offended is harder to be won than a strong city: and their contentions are like the bars of a castle.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "A man’s belly shall be satisfied with the fruit of his mouth; and with the increase of his lips shall he be filled.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Death and life are in the power of the tongue: and they that love it shall eat the fruit thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Whoso findeth a wife findeth a good thing, and obtaineth favour of the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "The poor useth intreaties; but the rich answereth roughly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:18:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "A man that hath friends must shew himself friendly: and there is a friend that sticketh closer than a brother.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 18:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:18:24"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
